From 6df15cad374aba361c366db755e0b233306d0795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:32:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/33] WIP: dream2lte charger: cable type, current limits,
 battery temperature

MAX77865 charger:
- the charger watchdog, enabled by the bootloader, was never cleared
  and turned charging off ~95 s after the last clear: the phone ran
  from the battery while plugged in. It is now cleared from the 5 s
  poll (so charging still stops if the system hangs).
- the charger type found by the MUIC's BC1.2 detection sets the input
  limit and charge current, with the vendor kernel's values: SDP
  500/500 mA, CDP 1500/1500 mA, DCP 1800 mA in / 2100 mA charge
  (capped by the monitored battery's constant-charge-current-max).
- battery temperature from the "battery-thermal" zone, with the vendor
  kernel's ranges: below 0 C and from 50 C charging stops, below 15 C
  800 mA, from 41 C 1250 mA and 4.15 V; with hysteresis. Without a
  temperature, charging is limited to 500 mA.
- float voltage and termination current from the monitored battery.
- usb_type, health, charge_type, input_current_limit and
  constant_charge_current (writable caps), charge_behaviour (auto /
  inhibit-charge) properties.
- settings are checked and restored on every poll.

DT: ADC node (bus clock is a hardware auto-gated BUSC gate, not
modelled, oscclk as a placeholder), NTC thermistors on ADC channels 4
(battery), 3 (charger) and 1 (USB connector) through
generic-adc-thermal with the vendor table, thermal zones with critical
trips, simple-battery node (3500 mAh, 2.1 A, 4.35 V, 150 mA term).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
